##Readme

## Project OverView
This repository contains our 340W course project, which focuses on numerical reasoning and question answering over financial documents using the FinQA dataset.

Our project explores how machine learning models handle deep, multi-step financial reasoning tasks and evaluates their performance compared to expert-level human reasoning


## About FinQA
FinQA is a large-scale dataset designed to advance research in financial question answering. It consists of:

Question–Answer pairs derived from real financial reports

Questions written by financial experts

Gold reasoning programs annotated for full explainability

Complex, multi-step numerical reasoning tasks

Unlike general-domain QA datasets, FinQA emphasizes:

Financial knowledge understanding

Numerical computation

Reasoning across tables and textual data

The dataset highlights that even large, pre-trained models significantly underperform compared to expert humans when handling financial reasoning tasks.

## GOAL
Understand challenges in financial numerical reasoning

Analyze how well existing models perform on FinQA

Explore explainability using annotated reasoning programs

Gain hands-on experience working with real-world financial data

Apply concepts from 340W to a practical, research-oriented problem
